---
import Storefront from '@/layouts/Storefront.astro';
import { getCatalogue } from '@/lib/api';

const { banners } = await getCatalogue();
---

<Storefront
  title="How it is made — Crochet & Co."
  description="What crochet actually involves, why handmade crochet costs what it does, and what happens to a piece once it is finished."
  banners={banners}
>
  <div class="shell shell--prose">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1 class="page-title">How it is made</h1>
      <p class="lede measure-wide">
        Crochet is one continuous thread, worked with a single hook. There is no
        knitting needle, no machine, and no seam unless I put one there. Everything
        follows from that.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="chain-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="prose">
      <section>
        <h2>What a round actually involves</h2>
        <p>
          A bag might be sixteen granny squares, and each square is four rounds of
          turning, chaining and pulling through. A round ends with an increase —
          working two stitches into one so the fabric stays flat instead of spiralling
          in on itself. Miss the count on one round and the whole thing tapers. That
          is the part nobody sees and everybody pays for.
        </p>
        <p>
          I keep a count on a scrap of paper beside the work. Not because I cannot
          remember, but because on round eleven of a square I should be thinking about
          how the strap will look, not whether I put a stitch in at the corner.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Why there are no machines</h2>
        <p>
          Machine knitting can produce a bag quickly and cheaply. It cannot produce
          this one: the slightly irregular tension where a colour changes, the place
          where two squares meet and one is a little tighter than the other. Those are
          not defects. They are the evidence that a person made it, and once you have
          handled something made that way you find the machine version a bit flat.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything here is worked in runs of one to ten. That is not marketing, it
          is arithmetic — there is only so much I can finish in a week alongside a
          full-time job, and I would rather make fewer things properly.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Yarn, and why it matters</h2>
        <p>
          Cotton everywhere, almost always. Cotton takes a stitch crisply, does not
          stretch when it is warm, and can be washed without a care label that
          terrifies people. Raffia for the summer bags, because it holds a shape
          beautifully and feels like the season it was made for.
        </p>
        <p>
          Yarn is the largest single cost in anything I make, and the reason a
          four-hour bag costs what it costs. I would rather tell you that than have
          you wonder.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What happens when it is finished</h2>
        <p>
          Blocking, which is the part everybody skips: a short soak, pinned to shape,
          and left to dry flat. It is what turns a slightly wonky pouch into something
          that stands up on its own. Then a photo, a piece of tissue, and the post.
        </p>
        <p>
          If something is not right when it arrives, tell me. I will repair it without
          charge, always, and the yarn is often still in the basket.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <aside class="cta-block panel panel--blush">
      <p class="cta-text">Anything here you would like in different colours?</p>
      <a class="btn-stitch" href="/custom-orders/">Start an enquiry</a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Storefront>

<style>
  .page-head { padding-block: 2.5rem 1.25rem; }

  .page-title {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: var(--text-section);
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 50, 'WONK' 1, 'opsz' 60;
  }

  .lede {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .prose { padding-block: 1.5rem; display: grid; gap: 2.25rem; }

  .prose h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 45, 'WONK' 1, 'opsz' 40;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .prose p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .cta-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .cta-text {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: 'SOFT' 40, 'WONK' 1, 'opsz' 30;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
